# Start here — {{KB_NAME}}

> Auto-generated at the end of deployment. Read this once.

## How to talk to the AI

Start every new chat with **«Используй AGENTS.md как основную инструкцию»**
(or: `Use AGENTS.md as the primary instruction`).

In Codex and Cursor the file is already auto-loaded, but the line costs
almost nothing and covers the three cases where that load silently fails:
the combined AGENTS.md budget is full (32 KiB across every file Codex
reads), `AGENTS.override.md` is sitting in the project root, or you started
the agent from a subdirectory that has its own `AGENTS.md`. In chatbots
(claude.ai, a ChatGPT project) there is no auto-load at all — there the
line is required.

## Commands you can use in chat

After the agent has read `AGENTS.md`, these commands work:

| Command | What it does | Cost |
|---------|--------------|------|
| `!status` | Say what is pending: review backlog, files waiting for extraction, reflection due, heal items, index problems (from `STATUS.md`) | ~0.5K tokens |
| `!view` | Open the local read-only knowledge graph viewer (`!view status`, `!view stop`) | 0 tokens |
| `!save` | Save a session summary now (decisions, conclusions, processed materials) | ~2K tokens |
| `!reflect` | Synthesize higher-level insights from accumulated facts | ~15K tokens |
| `!meta-review` | Find patterns across saved session summaries not reviewed yet | ~5–15K tokens |
| `!audit` | Per-pack review in a fresh session (`.repomix/audit/<pack>__request.md`) | ~5–20K / pack |
| `!review` | Process the `review/` queues and the converted files still waiting for extraction: turn them into knowledge, ask for input where needed | ~5–30K tokens |
| `!populate` | Re-generate `DATA_PLACEMENT_EXAMPLES.md` (when you've changed your role YAML) | ~50 tokens |
| `!export` | Pack this base into a bundle for another machine | ~100 tokens |
| `!import` | Merge bundles waiting in `sync/inbox/` | ~200 tokens |
| `!merge` | Finish an import: resolve conflicts, check contradictions, cross-link the new knowledge | ~5–40K tokens |
| `!heal` | Catch up after an upgrade (plan + auto fixes + assisted queue). See `kb-docs/18_HEAL.md` | ~0–40K tokens |
| `!refactor` | Two-step instruction trim (`kb-docs/17_REFACTOR.md`). Backup + eval. `--global` reports only | ~5–40K tokens |
| `!profile-review` | Interview `knowledge/profile/`: gaps first (3 questions), then stale facts | ~5–15K tokens |
| `!quiz` | Five questions about what is already in the base; costliest mistakes first | ~5–15K tokens |
| `!super` | Toggle operating mode: default ↔ super | 0 tokens |
| `!super on` / `!super off` | Force a mode | 0 tokens |
| `!super status` | Show current mode | 0 tokens |

## What is waiting for you: `STATUS.md`

Every reindex (manual, watcher or git hook) rewrites `STATUS.md` in this
folder: one line per thing that needs attention, each ending with the command
that resolves it — or `all clear`. The agent reads it at the start of a
session and tells you once what it lists; it acts only when you ask.

## How to run the watcher

The watcher auto-processes any file you drop into `raw/<sub>/unsorted/`.

### macOS
- **Start:** double-click `watcher-start.command` (in this folder)
- **Stop:** press Ctrl+C in the terminal window that opened

### Linux
- **Start:** `./shell/watcher.sh` from a terminal
- **Or background:** `./shell/watcher.sh --daemon` then `./shell/watcher.sh --stop` to stop

### Windows
- **Start:** double-click `watcher-start.bat`
- **Stop:** close the cmd window or Ctrl+C

## Manual reindex

If you didn't run the watcher and want to process accumulated raw files now:

- **macOS:** double-click `reindex.command`
- **Linux:** `./shell/reindex.sh`
- **Windows:** double-click `reindex.bat`

## Using this base on two computers

If you deployed this base on more than one machine, keep them in sync instead of
copying folders around:

1. **On the machine with new knowledge** — double-click `export.command`
   (macOS) / `export.bat` (Windows), or run `./shell/export.sh`. A `.zip` appears
   in `sync/outbox/`.
2. **Move that file** to the other machine's `sync/inbox/` folder.
3. **There** — double-click `import.command` / `import.bat`, or run
   `./shell/import.sh`.
4. **In the AI chat** — say `!merge`.

Nothing gets overwritten: new pages are added, identical ones are skipped, and
anything you changed on **both** machines is queued with a diff for the agent to
merge. Every touched file is backed up to `sync/backups/` first. Do it in both
directions and both machines end up with everything.

